  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For an array BBB of length MMM, consider partitioning the array into KKK non-intersecting subarrays, and then choosing KKK integers X1,X2,…,XKX_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_KX1​,X2​,…,XK​ and replacing all elements of the ithi^{th}ith subarray, say BjB_jBj​ with Bj⊕XiB_j \\oplus X_iBj​⊕Xi​, where ⊕\\oplus⊕ represents the bitwise XOR operator. Note that XiX_iXi​ can be an **arbitrary** non-negative integer.\n\nLet f(B)f(B)f(B) denote the **minimum** value of KKK such that there exists a partition of the array into KKK non-intersecting subarrays and a sequence of integers X1,X2,…,XKX_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_KX1​,X2​,…,XK​ such that the final array becomes **sorted** in non-decreasing order.\n\nFor example, let us take an array B=[2,1,1,2,3]B = [2, 1, 1, 2, 3]B=[2,1,1,2,3], we can choose K=2K = 2K=2, and partition the array into [[2],[1,2,2,3]][[2], [1, 2, 2, 3]][[2],[1,2,2,3]] and now choose X1=0X_1 = 0X1​=0, X2=4X_2 = 4X2​=4 to get [2,5,5,6,7][2, 5, 5, 6, 7][2,5,5,6,7]. Thus, we see that the final array is sorted. Further it can be shown that it is impossible to sort the array with K=1K = 1K=1. Hence f([2,1,2,2,3])=2f([2, 1, 2, 2, 3]) = 2f([2,1,2,2,3])=2.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of size NNN, and QQQ queries. For each query, given LLL and RRR, output f(A[L,R])f(A[L,R])f(A[L,R]) where A[L,R]A[L,R]A[L,R] represents the subarray from the LthL^{th}Lth index to the RthR^{th}Rth index, i.e. [AL,AL+1,…,AR][A_L, A_{L + 1}, \\ldots, A_R][AL​,AL+1​,…,AR​].\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two integers NNN and QQQ, the size of the array and the number of queries respectively.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN integers, A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe next QQQ lines each contain two integers, LLL and RRR, the parameters for this query.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each query, output on a new line, the value f(A[L,R])f(A[L,R])f(A[L,R]).",
